# Derived artifacts: a merge of two branches is never the answer for them.
#
# Every path below is written by `scripts/derive` out of canonical sources that git merges
# perfectly well. What conflicts is the *fingerprint* the generators stamp into the output —
# `Generated from canonical inputs <hash>`, `"source_hash": ...` — and that value is a
# function of the merged tree, so neither side's is right and no textual combination of them
# is either. Left to the default driver, every branch that touches a canonical file conflicts
# here, and the resolution is always the same gesture: take a side, run `scripts/derive`,
# stage the real answer. One branch open today has done it five times.
#
# `merge=derived` short-circuits the pretence. The driver (scripts/merge-derived) resolves to
# ours and exits clean, so the merge completes and the tree carries a *stale* derived file —
# which is exactly what the `derived-current` gate in .githooks/pre-commit refuses to let you
# commit (`scripts/pages current`, and `scripts/derive-check` behind it in CI). The staleness
# is caught by the thing built to catch staleness, one command later, instead of by hand
# inside a conflict marker.
#
# The driver has to be declared per clone — `git config merge.derived.driver ...`, which
# `just derive-merge-driver` does. Without that declaration git falls back to the default
# text merge and you get the conflicts you get today: this file makes merging better where it
# is wired and never worse where it is not.

docs/PLAN_STATUS.md                 merge=derived
docs/PAGES_STATUS.md                merge=derived
docs/SITE_CLAIMS.md                 merge=derived
docs/generated/**                   merge=derived
site/data/generated/**              merge=derived
site/data/registry/**               merge=derived
site/content/docs/pages-status.md   merge=derived
site/content/docs/plan-status.md    merge=derived
site/content/docs/site-claims.md    merge=derived

# The site's registry projection: one page per capability and per module, all of them
# rewritten whenever the registry moves.
site/content/registry/**            merge=derived

# The rest of what `majordomus generate` writes. The list above was the site and the
# status documents; these are the projections and the schema/allow-list outputs, and they
# conflict for exactly the same reason — a stamp or a fingerprint of the tree they were
# generated from. `test/cases/57_derived_merge_driver.sh` asks `git check-attr` about every
# path in docs/generated/artifacts.json, so this list cannot fall behind the generator:
# adding a generate target without a rule here fails the case.
AGENTS.md                             merge=derived
CLAUDE.md                             merge=derived
share/allow/**                        merge=derived
share/sections/**                     merge=derived
share/schemas/**/*.schema.json        merge=derived
